      },
      "value": "I have not yet owned a direct external enterprise-customer engagement on an ML/AI problem, so I would not want to overstate that. The closest analogue is stakeholder-facing ML work where the users were domain experts rather than ML engineers. At Columbia Zuckerman, after building self-supervised denoising workflows for two-photon calcium-imaging data, I organized the research code into a downloadable package and wrote step-by-step documentation for wet-lab researchers. I also presented survey-analysis findings to board members at the Columbia Asian Faculty Association. For Databricks AI FDE, I would bring that same habit of translating model behavior, evaluation tradeoffs, and implementation details into decisions a customer can act on, while continuing to build direct enterprise-facing experience.",
